e2e	End-to-end suite	2026-10-21T01:29:47.4377317Z         help[4]: "Open the PR: https://github.com/github.com/example/no-mistakes/pull/99","Summarize this pipeline run for the user in a concise, easily readable format: what was validated and what was found.","Commit post-pipeline follow-up work on top of the existing branch so every pipeline fix commit remains present. Never abort-and-restart, reset, or replace the branch in a way that drops prior gate-fix commits.","Before a post-pipeline local commit or fresh run, follow the exact structured `branch_sync.next_action.command`. A `sync` action may be a strict fast-forward or a content-equivalent diverged advance that anchors the pre-sync head before moving the branch with reset semantics. A `recover_custody` action may be ordinary `no-mistakes axi sync --recover` when unpublished pipeline commits are preserved in the local gate, or exact `no-mistakes axi sync --recover --keep-local` when a bound archive preserves a divergent later head while custody returns at the reported required head, when the mirror holds the preserved head but the worktree cannot safely adopt it, or when that preserved head is unavailable and you are explicitly discarding the missing commits; never substitute one recovery command for the other. A `release_binding` action runs exactly `no-mistakes axi sync --release` for a terminal run whose persisted push binding no longer matches the live remote: it anchors the pipeline heads, moves the local gate branch to the current head, and returns custody; it is mutually exclusive with recovery and archive binding and never force-pushes the changed remote. A `user_owned` state means cancellation released the branch before changing the submitted head: the exact branch and head are yours, immediately usable, and no sync action is needed. Process blocked or pipeline-owned states instead of improvising reset, stash, merge, rebase, force, or branch replacement."
